// FIX 4.4 grammar for the issue #132 case-study pilot.
//
// One SOH-delimited field per token (tag=value absorbs everything up to and
// including the SOH; anchored by the leading digits and the literal '='):
// values in the corpus never contain \x01 or \n. The field sequence merges
// binary, so long messages fold in log depth. Message-level semantics
// (8=FIX.4.4 first, 9=<body length> second, 10=<checksum> last, checksum =
// sum of the message bytes preceding "10=" mod 256, zero-padded) are checked
// identically over the resolved tokens and in the hand scanner.

Grammar: Fix44Pilot

<field> ::= /[0-9]+=[^\x01\n]+\x01/
<field_seq> ::= <field_seq> <field_seq> | <field>
